      "content": "1. INTRODUCTION TO AGRICULTURE"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Agriculture forms a critical foundation of the Indian economy and rural livelihood.",
        "Farming in India is broadly categorized into Subsistence Farming, Commercial Farming, and Plantation Farming.",
        "India's agricultural calendar is divided into three distinct cropping seasons: Kharif, Rabi, and Zaid.",
        "Modern agricultural progression relies heavily on irrigation infrastructure, agricultural marketing, and government initiatives.",
        "Land reforms and the Green Revolution represent pivotal structural changes in Indian agricultural history."
